Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:33:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs(memory): revise to additive relevance tier after review
 panel (a5ecc5aa)

Adversarial panel killed the v1 reorder: unbounded ts_rank scan (org scope
matches all rows before LIMIT), baseline-stability/guardrail-eviction
regression, multiplier math that out-levered relevance, and a silent
attribution rank-flip. Pivot to the audit's original two-tier intent: keep
Tier 1 (scope+recency baseline) byte-identical; add Tier 2, a bounded
FTS-ranked supplement (fts @@ + ts_rank, deduped, kind<>rule, own budget).
Additive structure lets the supplement use the GIN index (bounds the scan)
and dissolves the backward-compat and rank-flip attacks. No migration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
